00:10:10.060 --> 00:10:10.460
Everybody

00:10:12.915 --> 00:10:14.755
people would come build it and they'll come.

00:10:15.395 --> 00:10:16.755
After 2010,

00:10:16.755 --> 00:10:20.915
after the big financial crisis and all the banking reforms and everything else,

00:10:21.395 --> 00:10:23.635
it just became very, very difficult

00:10:23.875 --> 00:10:24.835
to do that.

00:10:25.315 --> 00:10:31.020
So from 2010 to the present, you've averaged about three to five permits per year.

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:37.420
So going from 20 to 35 to three to five from 2010 to 2022.

00:10:37.660 --> 00:10:53.575
So that's a real significant decline in building permits. So you're not having a lot of houses aren't being built. So it's very hard for us to say we should build, you know, 10 affordable housing units a year when the market is only building three or three to five houses per year.

00:10:54.135 --> 00:10:54.855
Next slide.

00:10:57.730 --> 00:11:12.605
